course: dictionary
lesson: 11666
title: Saying something is true
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When someone asserted something, they said it firmly, as if it was definitely true. Look for the clues: did they say it strongly and with confidence? «She asserted that she was innocent.» This tells you she firmly claimed she had done nothing wrong.
explain: Asserted is the past form of assert. Test the meaning by swapping in a simpler phrase. «Mia said firmly that the answer was correct» means the same as «Mia asserted that the answer was correct».
explain: Asserted can also mean standing up for yourself or using your rights clearly. «He asserted himself in the meeting and was finally heard.» In stories and maths, a claim that someone asserted may be right or wrong, so always check it for yourself.
fact: Asserted means said firmly that something is true.
fact: «She asserted that she was innocent» means she firmly claimed she had done nothing wrong.
fact: Asserted (yourself) means acting confidently so that people notice and respect you.
fact: Asserted (rights or power) means showing and using them clearly.
fact: A claim someone asserted is not always true, so check it before you believe it.
exercise: «The captain asserted that the ship was safe.» What does asserted mean here? | Said firmly that it was true | *Sailed the ship very slowly | Asked a question about the ship | Painted the ship in bright colours
exercise: «Tom asserted that 7 times 8 is 54.» Is Tom's statement right? | It is not a statement at all | *No, it is wrong, so check the sum | Yes, because it is a long number | Yes, because Tom asserted it
exercise: Ruby asserted herself in class by speaking up clearly. What does asserted (yourself) mean? | Fell asleep during the lesson | Wrote a letter to her teacher | Hid at the back of the room | *Acted confidently so people noticed her
test: «The witness asserted that he saw the car at nine o'clock.» Which word is closest in meaning to asserted? | *Claimed firmly | Forgot | Whispered | Doubted
test: Dad asserted his right to a quiet Sunday. What does asserted mean here? | Asked nicely for a cup of tea | *Showed and used his right clearly | Lost his right | Gave his right away
exam: Jayden reads, «The robot asserted that 2 plus 2 is 5.» What should he do? | Skip it, because numbers do not matter | Copy it into his book without thinking | *Check the sum, because a claim can be wrong | Believe it, because robots are always right
